			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4765259">
									

<p>So. When I read a story like this, the nonbinary pronouns tend to make me have a visceral reaction that's&#8230; It distracts me, and makes me think, &quot;Is it me necessary to have the character be like this?&quot;</p>
<p>But&#8230; That's the thing, isn't it. The fact that I'm trying to find justification in the the usage of these nonstandard pronouns is <em>exactly the problem.</em></p>
<p>It means that stories like this are so, so important because they continue to push the normalization of nonstandard pronouns, and I know eventually I won't even notice them.</p>
<p>(What's really ironic is that I have this reaction and <em>I myself am enby.</em>)</p>
<p>So, thank you. Thank you for pushing forward in the name of progress and tying it to a damn good story. &lt;3</p>

