<p>Eparch was used first in <a href="/scp-4015">SCP-4015</a> and is defined within that article as…</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;Eparch&quot; is an esoteric class denoting an object classed as an SCP for its anomalous circumstances or relationships rather than for having anomalous effects.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I decided against footnote-defining it because, like… well, it seems a bit tacky.</p>
<p>And yes, ze/hir are being used as nb; the &quot;their&quot; is used in reference to the general population in-context instead of just Lucian.</p>
<p>Glad you liked it!</p>

